   "design": "In s1 the teacher marks attendance on the learning environment roster on a tablet, so the spreadsheet typing in s2 drops. Final grades sync from the grade book to the student record system, and the teacher confirms the transfer, instead of entering them twice. The grade book's own views replace the separate spreadsheet. Students submit extension requests on a course form that records the decision and new deadline. Rules flag missing grades and attendance below the threshold before deadlines. The result report takes its statistics from the grade book and the teacher writes the commentary. Students see their own attendance and grades, so fewer record questions come by mail. Deciding extensions, checking flags, the report commentary and settling issues stay with the teacher.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "Attendance, grades and requests were kept in several places and entered twice.",
   "enabler_now": "Grade sync between the learning environment and the student record system, course forms and completeness rules.",
   "still_hard": "Grade changes after the sync.",
   "human_edge": "Judging whether a student's absence needs a conversation.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less double entry; record judgement stays.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "exam office",
     "task": "Publish results",
     "learn": "Whether grades arrive complete and on time."
    }
   ],
